 ## What a tower wears
 
+**The arrays (2026-10-19).** building.gdshader holds 20 tints (`RenderShapes.CITY_SLOTS`) and four facade types. A building's city code packs its tint (1 plus the tint, up to 31), 32 times its facade (4: the look's own windows), 256 for a lobby storey and 512 times the floor its crown starts at, in a 32-bit float texel. `city_check` covers the balconied facade's neighbours (its widest step 0.026 of relative luminance on Art's data of 2026-10-18; the budget 0.085). Before and after, both switches on in a scratch build: `img/city/tints20-before-after.png` (uncommitted).
+
 | Step | What | Where |
 | --- | --- | --- |
 | A | **Glass that takes the sky.** A tower's glass moves 40% toward the sky's colour in its direction, at the glass's own luminance, so no pane changes value. It goes blue at noon and warm under a sunset. A pane below the eye takes the sky half a screen over the horizon (the blue, not the pale band, and never the ground). | `building.gdshader` 7c; `RenderLook.GLASS_SKY` |
-| B | **One of Art's six tints of its look**, picked by the district's weights: the wall's three tones, its glass, bright glass and trim. | `RenderShapes.city_look`, `city_uniforms` |
