 The depth aids of the fight-lanes plan (`fight-lanes-render.md` section 4), besides the ground shadow. Both are drawn by the ground shader (`ground.gdshaderinc`), so neither costs a draw call, and both follow craters and slopes.
 
 - **The lane table** is the sim's: `S.lanes`, a flat packed array (`docs/world/fight-lanes-world.md` section 10), read through `render/core/lanes.gd`. The stand-in built from the plan's numbers is gone since World's lanes window (2026-10-11); a world with no table paints no streets. The re-laid city's look (shapes, district looks, row haze, avenues and paved lots) is in `lanes-look.md`.
-- **City variety** (2026-10-16, Orb's homework 4; `city-variety.md`). Art's tints, facade types, lobby storey and set-back crown on the downtown and mid-rise towers, and glass that takes the sky. Two switches, both off: `RenderLook.CITY_TINTS` (the sky glass and the tints; in full effects they made signaturecity and rushcity worse, 2026-10-17) and `CITY_FACADES` (the facade types, the lobby storey and the crown). `city_check.gd` holds every pair of neighbouring tones to the budget (Legal's w05, RL-144).
+- **City variety** (2026-10-16, Orb's homework 4; `city-variety.md`; 20 tints and a fourth facade, balconied, since 2026-10-19). Art's tints, facade types, lobby storey and set-back crown on the downtown and mid-rise towers, and glass that takes the sky. Two switches, both off: `RenderLook.CITY_TINTS` (the sky glass and the tints; in full effects they made signaturecity and rushcity worse, 2026-10-17) and `CITY_FACADES` (the facade types, the lobby storey and the crown). `city_check.gd` holds every pair of neighbouring tones to the budget (Legal's w05, RL-144).
 - **What the picture does not need** (2026-10-17, Performance's audit; `geometry-and-warmup.md`). The crowd is drawn in chunks the camera culls. A water chunk no water can reach is hidden. Every effect's shader is drawn once at boot, off-screen, so no first draw lands in a fight.
 - **Painted streets.** In a district the ground under the street lanes is painted by strip: sidewalks with slab joints, kerb parking with bay marks, and carriageways with a dashed centre line (`STREET_*`). The paint fades in over 120 units at a district's ends, lies under craters, rubble, cracks and scorch, and its thin lines fade out before they alias at far zoom. The district weight is found in the vertex stage (up to 16 districts); a pixel walks at most 16 strips (three streets of five), and on a sidewalk or a kerb the avenues, to open a crossing. `--nostreets` leaves the ground unpainted, for A/B. Avenues (the cross streets), crossings and the districts' own looks are in `lanes-look.md`.
 - **The lane cue.** A soft stripe on the ground, or on the water, at a fighter's depth, in his colour, 450 units each way along the street (`LANE_CUE_*`). It shows only while it says something: the two fighters are more than 40 units apart in depth, or his own depth is changing faster than 60 units a second. It comes up in 0.15 s and goes in 0.6 s, on tick time. It is never thinner than about a pixel. In today's sim that means during brunt launches only.
